1 CO TST-006 m=D | testing.md:24-26 restates TST-006 (WebApplicationFactory-based integration tests when routing, binding, middleware, auth, DI, repositories or persistence is the subject) at DEFAULT strength; loaded for test files (C9).
2 CD DEP-003 m=MN k=W st=S | check-manifests.js:126-127 marks '*' or empty versions as ERROR with no explicit-request branch (prerelease gets only WARN 'allowed only when explicitly requested'). DEP-003 allows floating versions when explicitly requested. Range specifiers (^, ~, [..]) are not flagged, so the checker is narrower than DEP-003 for ranges (no extra obligation there).
  x: '*' or empty NuGet/npm versions (and npm 'latest'/x) are checker errors even when the user explicitly requested a floating version
  s: User explicitly requests "*" for a dev tool: DEP-003 allows it; the M1 checker reports an ERROR finding owned by add-dependency.
  fhd: Whether a checker should honour DEP-003's explicit-request exception for floating versions.
3 IA m=M | MODULE.md leakTokens data plus check-instructions.js: instruction and enforcement files outside a capability's own facets must not name the selected implementation; this governs the instruction system's capability boundary, not product code.
4 MX | settings.json:7-12 registers pre-tool-use.js for every Bash/PowerShell call (onFailure block). The gate bundles enforcement of a canonical prohibition with candidate-specific gating.
  - CO DEP-025 m=MN d=WF | Gating peer-override commands (npm --force/--legacy-peer-deps) is the mechanism of DEP-025 (C3).
  - XW m=MN | Every Bash/PowerShell call passes through a pre-execution gate for dependency and project-reference commands (denied/asked per the gate's own rules; onFailure block = fail closed when the hook cannot run).
    s: Node.js is unavailable or the hook crashes: canonical policies allow running a plain `dotnet add package` after due diligence; M1's registration blocks the call (declared intent; host support for onFailure not executed).
    r: host support for exec-form args and onFailure:block not verified (C10)
5 CD TST-001 TST-005~ m=D k=P | TST-001 makes NUnit the default framework and TST-005 prefers explicit cases. The rule adds specific NUnit idioms: [TestFixture]/[Test], [SetUp]/[OneTimeSetUp] with matching teardown, Assert.That constraint assertions, and explicit case tables as [TestCase] rows rather than TestCaseSource generators.
  x: Assert.That constraint-model assertions; setup attributes paired with matching teardown; explicit case tables written as [TestCase] rows, not TestCaseSource
  s: NUnit tests using classic Assert.AreEqual and a TestCaseSource array of five explicit cases satisfy TST-001/TST-005 but deviate from M1's default conventions.
6 XW m=D | git-workflow SKILL.md:58-59 (and 70-71): follow the repository commit-message convention, otherwise Conventional Commits as a useful default; body for motivation/constraints/migration notes; do not narrate obvious diffs. No policy governs commit-message form (GOV-015/WF-022 cover whether and what to commit).
  t: when a commit is prepared (only on explicit request per GOV-015)
  e: an existing repository convention takes precedence
  s: In a repository without a convention the agent commits "update files": allowed by all 196 policies, contrary to M1's Conventional Commits default.
